course: dictionary
lesson: 10881
title: Vine
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A vine is a plant with a long, thin, bendy stem. Vines need something to hold on to, so they climb up walls, fences or trees, or spread along the ground. «Under the canopy lies the understorey, a dim world of young trees, shrubs, vines and big-leaved plants.» Here a vine is one kind of plant that grows in a dark part of the forest.
explain: Context clues help you check the meaning. «Example: a girl in Ohio gathers sticks for a campfire and spots a vine with three shiny leaves.» She spots it and it has leaves, so a vine is a living plant you can see growing, not a rope someone has left behind.
explain: The same word can mean different things. «Black, white and green peppercorns are the same berry of a climbing vine from India.» Here vine means the plant itself. «I heard it on the grapevine» uses the word in a different way, and it means news passed on by word of mouth. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it in. «In the jungle, explorers swing from vine to vine.» If you put "long hanging stem" in place of vine, the sentence still makes sense. That tells you your meaning is right.
fact: A vine is a plant with a long, thin, bendy stem.
fact: Vines climb up walls, fences or trees, or spread along the ground.
fact: A grapevine is the plant that grapes grow on.
fact: In a jungle, a vine is a long hanging stem that animals and explorers can swing on.
fact: «Rafflesia arnoldii» has the biggest single flower, and it lives as a parasite inside a vine.
exercise: «Under the canopy lies the understorey, a dim world of young trees, shrubs, vines and big-leaved plants.» What is a vine in this sentence? | A type of rock found in the forest | A tool for cutting branches | A kind of animal that lives in trees | *A plant with a long, bendy stem
exercise: «In the jungle, explorers swing from vine to vine.» What does vine mean here? | A type of jungle bird | *A long hanging stem | A stone wall in the jungle | A river that runs through the trees
exercise: Ella says a grapevine is a tree that grapes fall from. Which is right? | *A plant that grapes grow on | A bird that eats grapes | A tree that grapes fall from | A machine for picking grapes
test: «Black, white and green peppercorns are the same berry of a climbing vine from India.» What is a climbing vine? | *A plant that climbs up supports | A type of jungle explorer | A large animal from India | A kind of rope used by sailors
test: «Rafflesia has no leaves, stems or roots of its own and lives inside a vine as a parasite.» Where does Rafflesia live? | In a garden pond | *Inside a vine | On the forest floor with its own roots | Up in the branches of a tall tree with its own leaves
exam: Ali says, «I heard it on the grapevine that school is closed tomorrow.» What does grapevine mean here? | A kind of grape | A long rope in the jungle | A plant in the garden | *News passed on by word of mouth, a rumour
